@startuml
' InfluxDB Deployment: Centered View on Database, Service, and Token Secret
left to right direction

skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam backgroundColor #EEEBD

cloud "Kubernetes Cluster: capiot-cluster" {

    node "Namespace: capiot" {

        node "Configuration & Secrets" {
            component "InfluxDB Token Generation (kubectl exec)" as Token_Generator
            artifact "Kubernetes Secret: influxdb-api-token" as InfluxDB_Token_Secret
        }

        node "InfluxDB Internal Exposure" {
            component "InfluxDB Service (ClusterIP)" as InfluxDB_Service
        }

        node "InfluxDB Database Deployment" {
            database "influxdb-deployment StatefulSet (1/1)" as InfluxDB_Deployment
        }
    }
}

' Relationships
Token_Generator --> InfluxDB_Deployment : "Exec into Pod (Generate Token)"
InfluxDB_Token_Secret <-- Token_Generator : "Stores Generated Token"

InfluxDB_Service --> InfluxDB_Deployment : "Exposes Pods Internally"

' Notes
note top of InfluxDB_Token_Secret
  Contains:
  - api-token: <Generated Token>
  Used by applications
  (e.g., api-influxdb-deployment)
  to access InfluxDB API.
end note

note right of InfluxDB_Service
  Type: ClusterIP
  Internal Service for
  InfluxDB database access
  within the cluster.
  Accessed by other services
  like 'api-influxdb-deployment'.
end note

note bottom of InfluxDB_Deployment
  Time-Series Database
  Data Persistence:
  Uses Persistent Volumes
end note

note bottom of Token_Generator
  Manual / CI/CD Step:
  Uses `kubectl exec <pod-name> -- influx auth create ...`
  to generate an API token for a
  specific user/bucket access.
  This token is then retrieved
  and stored into the
  'influxdb-api-token' Secret.
end note

@enduml
